From ab1997f015218c2dc996831132b6faff871b2220 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Ewen <ryan.ewen@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 18:57:49 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] agentHost: brand the remote transport's two URI
 namespaces

`EditorRemoteAgentHostTransport` is the single point that converts directory
identities between the agent host's `file:` namespace and the window's
`vscode-remote:` one. Both conversions were typed `(uri: string) => string`,
so the two directions were interchangeable and a raw unconverted URI was
assignable wherever a converted one was expected. Neither mistake could fail
loudly: `ExtUri` comparisons gate on scheme, so a cross-namespace value
compares as a confident `false` rather than raising.

Give each direction a distinct branded string type and name the two mapping
directions once as fields, so picking the wrong direction, or passing a value
that was never converted, is a compile error.

No behaviour change.
