From 1dd09ff3ddec5b44c3f1e519de0cb1beb1704eea Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Ewen <ryan.ewen@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 19:00:22 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] agentHost: convert a session's project root at the remote
 transport

`EditorRemoteAgentHostTransport` already rewrites a session's working
directories between the host's `file:` namespace and the window's
`vscode-remote:` one, but it left `SessionMetadata.project.uri` alone. In a
dev container the two fields of the same session therefore arrived in
different namespaces, and every consumer that compares them silently saw no
match:

- `agentHostSessionListStore` dropped a legacy worktree session from the list
  in a window opened on its repository, because the project root it matches on
  was still `file:`.
- `agentHostSessionHandler._inheritWorktreeTrust` found no worktree under the
  repository root, so it re-prompted for a worktree the user already trusted.
- `agentHostSessionWorkspace` never found the primary working directory equal
  to the project root, so an ordinary session rendered as worktree-isolated.

Map `project.uri` in `_mapDirectories`, which every carrier of that field
already flows through: `listSessions`, `root/sessionAdded`,
`root/sessionSummaryChanged`, and the `initialize`/`subscribe`/`reconnect`
snapshots. No action mutates `project`, so those carriers are the complete
set. The conversion is unambiguous because `project` is host-owned: the value
only ever originates from the host on the other end of this connection.

The session list's containment guard admitted `file:` project roots only,
which after this change would exclude exactly the ones that now match. Widen
it to the schemes that can name a workspace folder, keeping repository URLs
such as `https://host/owner/repo` excluded and reported.
